  "text": ".compile\n.compile\n\n.compileThe expression $a^4+b^4$ can be written as $(a^2+b^2)^2 - 2ab(a^2+b^2)$. Since $a^2+b^2$ is a root of the equation, we have $a^2+b^2=p-aq$. Substituting this into the expression, we get:\n\n$(a^2+b^2)^2 - 2ab(a^2+b^2) = (p-aq)^2 - 2aq(p-aq) = p^2-2pq-a^2q^2$.\n\nWe are given that $a^4+b^4=22$, so we can substitute this into the expression to get:\n\n$p^2-2pq-a^2q^2 = 22$.\n\nWe are also given that $p=a+b$ and $q=ab$, so we can substitute these into the expression to get:\n\n$p^2-2pq-q^2 = (a+b)^2-2(a+b)ab-(ab)^2 = a^2+b^2-2ab=a^2+b^2-2ab=a^2+b^2-2(q-0)$.\n\nSince we know $a^2+b^2=p-aq=q$, we can substitute this into the expression to get:\n\n$q = q-2q = -q$.\n\nThis means that $q=0$. Substituting this back into the equation $p^2-2pq-a^2q^2 = 22$, we get:\n\n$p^2-2pq = 22$.\n\nSince we know $q=0$, this simplifies to:\n\n$p^2 = 22$.\n\nTaking the square root of both sides, we get:\n\n$p = \\pm \\sqrt{22}$.\n\nSince $a^2+b^2=p-aq$, we know that $a^2+b^2=p$, so we can substitute this into the equation $p = \\pm \\sqrt{22}$ to get:\n\n$p = \\sqrt{22}$.\n\nTherefore, the values of $p$ and $q$ are $\\boxed{\\sqrt{22} \\text{ and } 0}$, respectively.",
